meta {
  name: Sim route for an unsaved shape
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/courses/sim-route
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "roundingM": 30,
    "startLine": { "ax": -40, "ay": 0, "bx": 40, "by": 0 },
    "finishLine": { "sameAs": "start" },
    "marks": [
      { "x": 0, "y": 500, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" },
      { "x": 0, "y": 0, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" },
      { "x": 0, "y": 500, "r": 30, "side": "P", "type": "mark" }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  200 { roundingM, key, wps:[{x,y,kind,side?,ref?}], passes:[{label,index,kind,required,crossSide,crossed,entryCrossed,ok,scored,dist,point,entryPoint,centre,trav,entry}] }
  400 { error }

  Compiles the scripted route for a shape the editor is still working on,
  so the course builder can draw exactly what the simulator will sail
  (todo 32). Nothing is stored: same compiler as GET /courses/:id/sim-route
  and as the run generator.

  Validation is the course validation (a startLine and a finishLine are
  required, 1..10 marks, radius 5..200m) — a lineless course has no route.

  `passes` is the read-out the editor shows: per mark which side of the exit
  traverse the boat cuts on the way to the next mark (`crossSide` vs
  `required`, right of the axis facing the next mark = the boat passes right
  of the buoy = P, CCW), whether the entry traverse was cut arriving
  (`entryCrossed`, the approach latch), and the crossing point (`point`).
  `ok`/`scored` is what the device will score: cut toward the next mark on
  the declared side. Gates score by cutting the segment between the buoys.
  There are no distance minima anywhere: `dist` is informative only.
}
